      "description": "SUBSCRIBE_NAMESPACE carrying AUTHORIZATION_TOKEN twice, with different Token Values. The parameter's own definition is the carve-out: \"The AUTHORIZATION TOKEN parameter MAY be repeated within a message as long as the combination of Token Type and Token Value are unique after resolving any aliases.\" The second instance is written as a Type Delta of 0, which is the only encoding a second instance has once Section 10.2 requires ascending order. Identical to the with-auth-token vector with the count raised and a second token appended, so the only new bytes are the repeat itself.",
